			],
			"Message": "feat(Cocoon): Implement Language and Window API handlers and registries\n\nAdd foundational support for VS Code extension API compatibility in the Cocoon extension host by implementing shared logic for language provider registration and window event management.\n\nKey additions include:\n- **Language Provider Handler**: `RegisterProvider` creates auto-assigned handles, notifies Mountain via gRPC (`Context.SendToMountain`), and returns a disposable to unregister providers. It gracefully handles null/undefined inputs to support feature-flagged extensions.\n- **URI Key Utility**: `UriKey` normalizes URI objects, POJOs, and strings into stable map keys, preventing diagnostic collisions when multiple files are processed.\n- **Window Event Subscriber**: `MakeEventSubscriber` wraps `Context.Emitter` to provide standard `(listener, thisArg?, disposables?)` event subscription functions, ensuring correct `this` binding for class methods.\n- **Window Provider Registries**: `Registry` exports centralized `Map` instances for Tree Data, Webview View, Custom Editor, and Webview Panel providers. These allow efficient O(1) lookups by numeric handle or view ID, synchronizing state between the Cocoon runtime and Mountain requests.\n\nThese changes enable the extension host to manage VS Code-compliant providers and events, bridging the gap between extension code and the native Mountain backend.",
			"SHA": "5aaeeb7024a8e1c5a1bf474d2822fc9674fa832c"
		},
		{
